### Step 4: Structured JSON Logging

Logs must be structured JSON to stdout so Vector can parse and route to VictoriaLogs.

**Java (Dropwizard/Spring Boot):**

Add `logstash-logback-encoder` to `pom.xml`:
```xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>net.logstash.logback</groupId>
  <artifactId>logstash-logback-encoder</artifactId>
  <version>7.4</version>
</dependency>
```

Configure `logback.xml`:
```xml
<configuration>
  <appender name="STDOUT" class="ch.qos.logback.core.ConsoleAppender">
    <encoder class="net.logstash.logback.encoder.LogstashEncoder">
      <includeMdcKeyName>loggingId</includeMdcKeyName>
      <includeMdcKeyName>operation</includeMdcKeyName>
      <includeMdcKeyName>feature</includeMdcKeyName>
    </encoder>
  </appender>
  <root level="INFO">
    <appender-ref ref="STDOUT"/>
  </root>
</configuration>
```

Required fields: `timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `logger`, `operation`.

**Python:** Use `structlog` with JSON renderer.
**Go:** Use `log/slog` with `slog.NewJSONHandler(os.Stdout, nil)`.

Logging pattern for new code (per `coding-instructions.mdc`): add `feature=<tag>` only to new code, only where it proves the feature worked.

